          %h2#definition_of_hocat Definition of Ho(Cat)
          %p
            %strong Ho(Cat)
            is a name for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
          %ul
            %li
              whose objects are (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"}> small
              ) categories, and
            %li
              whose morphisms are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              classes of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
          %p
            This is an instance of a general construction which, given a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-category"} n-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
            with the same objects and whose morphisms are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            classes of 1-morphisms in the original
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncation"} truncation
            and denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_1
          %p
            It can also be viewed as an instance of the homotopy category of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            (or more generally a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
            as defined above is equivalent to the category obtained from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            by forcing all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences+of+categories"} equivalences of categories
            to be isomorphisms (by
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localizing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hTop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hTop
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            classes of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+maps"} continuous maps
            is equivalent to the category obtained from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            by inverting the homotopy equivalences (namely, the existence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+objects"} cylinder objects
            and/or
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+objects"} path objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
            for a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \times I
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is the category with two objects 0 and 1 and an isomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            of functors with the respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure"} canonical model structure
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
          %h2#subcategories_of_hocat Subcategories of Ho(Cat)
          %p
            Some notable full subcategories of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
            include
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Gpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Gpd)
              , the homotopy category of the category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gpd"} Gpd
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+1-types"} homotopy 1-types
            %li
              The category whose objects are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
              and whose morphisms are
              = succeed "es" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+class"} conjugacy class
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Gpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Gpd)
              whose objects are the connected groupoids. This category sometimes arises in the study of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbes"} gerbes
          %h2#hocatcategories Ho(Cat)-categories
          %p
            Like the homotopy category of any model category,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
            = succeed "-category\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
          %ul
            %li
              a collection of objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z
            %li
              for each pair of objects, a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(x,y)
            %li
              for each object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_x\in C(x,x)
            %li
              for each triple of objects, a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(y,z)\times C(x,y)\to C(x,z)
          %p
            such that the usual associativity and unit diagrams for an enriched category commute up to isomorphism. The difference between a
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            is that in a
            = succeed "-category," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
            %em no coherence axioms
            are required of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitor"} unitor
            isomorphisms; they are merely required to
            = succeed "." do
              %em exist
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
          %p
            Although
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
          %ul
            %li
              Any
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Cat
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
              = succeed "-category," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Cat
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
            %li
              Any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
              between bicategories which induces an equivalence of underlying
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Cat
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
          %p
            An example of a
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/346613"} this MathOverflow answer
          %h2#OtherLimits Other limits and colimits
          %p
            Although
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
            has products and coproducts, like most homotopy categories it is not well-endowed with other
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Gpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Gpd)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
          %p
            Consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 3
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi j
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi i
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{&amp;&amp; \mathbb{Z}/3\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^j\\
                  \\mathbb{Z}/2 &amp; \underset{i}{\to} &amp; S_3}
          %p
            where the two arrows are inclusions of subgroups. That is, we choose a 2-cycle and a 3-cycle in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a=(1,2)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b=(1,2,3)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/3
            with the subgroups generated by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            respectively. Regard these groups as connected groupoids and thus as objects of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 3
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi j
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi i
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{P &amp; \overset{f}{\to} &amp; \mathbb{Z}/3\\
                  ^g \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^j\\
                  \\mathbb{Z}/2 &amp; \underset{i}{\to} &amp; S_3}
          %p
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Gpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Gpd)
          %p
            Note that for any category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)(1,C)
            is the set of isomorphism classes of objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            is the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Cat)
            must induce pullbacks of sets of isomorphism classes of objects, and so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            must also have only one isomorphism class of objects; i.e. it must be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\to \mathbb{Z}/2
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\to \mathbb{Z}/3
            representing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi j
                    %mi f
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi i
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma\colon j f \cong i g
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma\in S_3
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msup
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(f(c)) = \sigma \cdot i(g(c)) \cdot \sigma^{-1}
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in P
          %p
            Now let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-pullback"} 2-pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Q
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi h
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 3
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi j
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi i
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mn 3
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{Q &amp; \overset{h}{\to} &amp; \mathbb{Z}/3\\
                  ^k \downarrow &amp; \cong &amp; \downarrow^j\\
                  \\mathbb{Z}/2 &amp; \underset{i}{\to} &amp; S_3.}
          %p
            Then the objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            are the elements of
            = succeed "," do
